[size=4][b]Kingmaker Tactics[/b][/size]
[i]Make Companions Smart Again.[/i]

Dragon Age: Origins-style tactics for your party in Pathfinder: Kingmaker. Give each companion a priority-ordered list of rules — [i]"if an ally drops below 35% HP, heal them"[/i], [i]"if a humanoid enemy has a weak Will save, cast Hold Person on it"[/i] — and the mod plays them out for you every few seconds in real-time combat: casting spells, using quick-slot items, toggling songs and stances, and picking attack targets.

A port of [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/pathfinderwrathoftherighteous/mods/1005]Wrath Tactics[/url] to Kingmaker (Enhanced Plus Edition).

[size=3][b]New to the mod? Start here[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Press [b]Ctrl+T[/b] (or click the helmet button in the bottom-left corner) to open the tactics panel.
[*]Open the [b]Packs[/b] tab: six ready-made role packs are waiting — Frontline, Healer, Bard, Arcane Caster, Archer, Skirmisher.
[*]Switch to a companion's tab and click [b]+ Apply Pack[/b] — e.g. the Bard pack on Linzi, the Healer pack on Harrim.
[*]Start a fight. That's it — tweak, reorder or delete rules whenever you like.
[/list]

[size=3][b]Highlights[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Priority-ordered rules[/b] per companion, plus Global rules for the whole party. The first rule whose conditions match wins.
[*][b]Compound conditions[/b] — AND inside a group, OR between groups. Conditions on enemies and allies apply to the [i]same[/i] unit, so "an enemy below 50% HP that is humanoid" means exactly that.
[*][b]Rich conditions[/b] — HP %, AC, saves, spell DC minus the target's save, attack bonus minus AC, buffs and debuffs, Paralyzed/Stunned/Frightened/..., creature type, alignment, hit dice, who is targeting whom, flanking, range brackets, spell slots, combat rounds and more.
[*][b]Actions[/b] — Cast Spell (with fallback chain), Cast Ability, Use Item, Toggle (songs, Rage, Power Attack, ...), Attack, [b]Heal[/b] (picks the best heal from spells, wands, potions and scrolls), Throw Splash Weapon, Move to Target, Switch Weapon Set.
[*][b]Smart targeting[/b] — lowest-HP ally, weakest-Will enemy, densest enemy group, biggest threat, or exactly the unit that matched your condition.
[*][b]Six default role packs[/b] with a real game plan each — openers (Haste, Prayer, Bless), crowd control by save, buffs on the ally who is being attacked, finishing blows, intercepting enemies that go for your casters. Rules a character can't perform yet are simply skipped.
[*][b]Presets and Packs[/b] — save rules as presets, bundle them into colour-coded packs, apply them to anyone, share them via clipboard export/import.
[*][b]Portrait badges[/b] — a small [b]T[/b] on every party portrait switches tactics on or off for that character with one click.
[*][b]You stay in charge[/b] — when you tell a companion to move or cast something, their rules wait until your order is done.
[*][b]Out-of-combat rules[/b] — opt a rule in to keep long buffs up between fights.
[*][b]5 languages[/b] — English, German, French, Russian, Chinese.
[/list]

[size=3][b]Good to know[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Real-time combat only.[/b] Tactics pause while turn-based mode is active.
[*][b]Items follow Kingmaker's rules:[/b] in combat a character can only use items from their own [b]quick slots[/b]. Put the potions, wands and flasks a companion should use mid-fight into their quick slots.
[*][b]Area spells are off by default[/b] in the Arcane pack (Fireball, Lightning Bolt) — the mod can't see your own melee in the blast radius.
[*][b]Buff Bot[/b] works fine alongside. If you enable Buff Bot's "cast buffs on combat start", give your tactics buff rules a "missing buff" condition, otherwise both mods cast the same buff.
[*]Each session writes its own log to [i]Mods/KingmakerTactics/Logs/[/i] — please attach it to bug reports.
[/list]

[size=3][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/site/mods/21]Unity Mod Manager[/url] (0.23.0+) for Pathfinder: Kingmaker.
[*]Drag the downloaded zip onto the UMM window (or extract it into [i]{GameDir}/Mods/KingmakerTactics/[/i]).
[*]Start the game.
[/list]

Requires Pathfinder: Kingmaker – Enhanced Plus Edition 2.1.7 or newer.

